From a8813278f5cabc68d9cf39b655342b85de7a4c35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fluorite Integration Role
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] shell: allow black curtain as background fallback

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local debug/integration behavior]

The local shell patch stack currently defers pending desktop surfaces until a
real BG role surface exists. That blocks NORMAL apps on images where no
homescreen/background client is started, even though agl-compositor already
has a built-in black curtain fallback and activation code that can use it as
the visible background.

Treat a mapped black curtain as sufficient background readiness so pending
surfaces can proceed without introducing an extra BG app dependency.
---
 src/shell.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/shell.c b/src/shell.c
index 7e0f7d8..1f8f9af 100644
--- a/src/shell.c
+++ b/src/shell.c
@@ -1066,6 +1066,8 @@
 		if (output->background &&
 		    output->background->role == IVI_SURFACE_ROLE_BACKGROUND)
 			return true;
+		if (output_has_black_curtain(output))
+			return true;
 	}
 
 	return false;
-- 
